<section class="section section-alt" id="vs-brands">
    <div class="container">
        <div class="section-header">
            <span class="section-label">Brand Intelligence</span>
            <h2>JP Medics vs. <span class="underline">Other Premium Brands</span></h2>
            <p>An honest, directional comparison framework for buyers who are actively comparing JP Medics with alternatives.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="brand-compare-grid">
            <div class="brand-row">
                <div class="brand-label"><div class="brand-name">JP Medics</div><div class="brand-vs">vs. Osaki</div></div>
                <div class="brand-body"><p>Osaki offers a significantly broader model range with strong feature density at each tier. JP Medics is more curated and precision-focused. Osaki tends toward more assertive intensity and broader feature coverage; JP Medics leans toward measured, sensor-led personalization. Buyers who want a large selection or prefer stronger pressure often choose Osaki. Buyers who want a more refined, precise feel in a Japanese flagship tier often prefer JP Medics.</p><div class="brand-verdict">JP Medics: more precise · Osaki: more choice and intensity</div></div>
            </div>
            <div class="brand-row">
                <div class="brand-label"><div class="brand-name">JP Medics</div><div class="brand-vs">vs. Infinity</div></div>
                <div class="brand-body"><p>Infinity competes well on technology breadth and value positioning. JP Medics competes on precision and Japanese positioning. Infinity tends to offer more features per dollar across a wider range; JP Medics delivers a more curated, refined experience at the flagship tier. Buyers who prioritize technology access at multiple price points often lean Infinity; buyers who want a more specialized, sensor-led Japanese approach tend toward JP Medics.</p><div class="brand-verdict">JP Medics: more curated · Infinity: broader technology access</div></div>
            </div>
            <div class="brand-row">
                <div class="brand-label"><div class="brand-name">JP Medics</div><div class="brand-vs">vs. Ogawa</div></div>
                <div class="brand-body"><p>Ogawa competes directly with JP Medics in the premium Japanese-heritage segment. Their Master Drive Duo flagship is a strong competitor to the KaZe Duo in particular — both offer dual-engine approaches, AI personalization, and refined Japanese design philosophy. Ogawa's design identity leans more minimalist; JP Medics' Chair Doctor AI is a distinctive differentiator. Both are premium choices in the same buyer tier.</p><div class="brand-verdict">Very close competition — try both in person to decide</div></div>
            </div>
            <div class="brand-row">
                <div class="brand-label"><div class="brand-name">JP Medics</div><div class="brand-vs">vs. Fujiiryoki</div></div>
                <div class="brand-body"><p>Fujiiryoki is the world's original massage chair manufacturer with over 70 years of Japanese engineering heritage. Both brands share a Japanese precision philosophy but express it differently: Fujiiryoki is more therapeutically focused (deep relief, quad heat, dual robots for coverage), while JP Medics is more sensor-driven and personalization-forward. Buyers who want the deepest therapeutic coverage often prefer Fujiiryoki; buyers who want more intelligent real-time adaptation often prefer JP Medics.</p><div class="brand-verdict">JP Medics: sensor-led AI · Fujiiryoki: therapeutic depth</div></div>
            </div>
            <div class="brand-row">
                <div class="brand-label"><div class="brand-name">JP Medics</div><div class="brand-vs">vs. Cozzia</div></div>
                <div class="brand-body"><p>Cozzia offers a broader lineup including dual-mechanism Duo models with competitive technology at various price points. Cozzia tends to deliver stronger compression coverage (VarioMotion™, high airbag counts); JP Medics delivers stronger AI personalization and sensor precision. Both are solid choices in the $10K–$16K premium segment with distinct engineering approaches.</p><div class="brand-verdict">JP Medics: AI precision · Cozzia: compression and track coverage</div></div>
            </div>
            <div class="brand-row">
                <div class="brand-label"><div class="brand-name">JP Medics</div><div class="brand-vs">vs. Bodyfriend</div></div>
                <div class="brand-body"><p>Bodyfriend is a South Korean luxury brand known for exceptional design, premium materials, and sophisticated AI health monitoring. Both brands operate in the same premium segment and appeal to similar buyer profiles — design-conscious, technology-forward, health-committed. JP Medics positions with more session-adaptive precision; Bodyfriend with more premium design identity and enveloping comfort.</p><div class="brand-verdict">Both premium — different design and massage philosophies</div></div>
            </div>
        </div>
        <div class="expert-callout" style="margin-top:28px">
